SUMMARY (what this experiment delivers, honestly):
================================================================================
  (i)   Theorem 1s target Y is now a COMPUTED number (held-out KRR MSE of the
        frozen at-init weight-only NTK), not just a described object.
  (ii)  R2(F->Y) = 0.8112 (rank-CV) / 0.6645 (L2 in-sample): the variance of Y explained
        by the finite label-free dictionary. NOT a "lower bound on R^2_cap"; full-Phi
        R^2_cap = 1 (vacuous). This is the only non-vacuous quantity (FIX-1).
  (iii) Sanity (tautological): NTK-Gram spectral features predict Y well (best ntkG_Ralpha_8.0 = 0.5005).
        Non-tautological (FIX-3): family gap spectral-vs-gradient cached proxies = GRADIENT family wins (CI excludes 0).
  (iv)  Coherence/lazy test (FIX-4): R2(F->Y)=0.8112 vs R2(F->acc)=0.8854; Spearman(Y,acc)=0.397
        -> the at-init NTK ceiling does NOT govern trained accuracy (NB201 not lazy).
  Single benchmark axis (NB201-TSS / CIFAR-10); cross-space story unaffected/unclaimed.

